From 80a3ab31eb108a5515ecaea0f4799a035b7d1ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JingMatrix <jingmatrix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:53:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Implement mount view hiding for isolated processes

Isolated and app-zygote processes can read peer and self mount tables
(AID_READPROC + hidepid bypass), and Android 17 zygote_next native children
read their own mountinfo from init's global namespace. Both expose module
mounts, which unmount-based hiding cannot cover in a shared namespace.

Filter the per-record show() output of /proc/<pid>/{mountinfo,mounts,
mountstats}, keyed on the reading task, by patching the .open slot of the
three proc file_operations to swap in a filtering show. A record is hidden
when its rendered text carries a module marker, when it matches the umount
list, or when the mount's real root dentry path lives under /data/adb; the
last covers /proc/mounts and mountstats, whose format omits the root field.
Filtering (not unmounting) is safe in the global namespace and keeps every
view of a given reader consistent, so the differential probe cannot fire.

The hide predicate is independent of ksu_module_mounted (modules may be
mounted outside KernelSU, e.g. NeoZygisk) and covers the app-zygote isolated
uid range (90000-98999) as well as the regular one. Exposed as a
manager-toggleable feature (KSU_FEATURE_MOUNT_HIDE); the kernel_umount path
is kept for classic private-namespace apps. Samsung no-patch-text builds use
kretprobe return handlers on proc mount-file opens and update only the
per-file show callback, avoiding global file_operations writes.
